 on node1 (Alpine, ext4 root has no native snapshot support) by installing btrfs-progs, creating a loopback-backed btrfs filesystem with a 'data' subvolume mounted at /srv/data (persisted via /etc/fstab). Populated /srv/data with app files, took a read-only btrfs snapshot as baseline, modified the live directory (edit/delete/add), then restored /srv/data to the exact baseline snapshot content via subvolume swap, verified byte-identical via sha256 manifest diff. Completed the mandatory restart protocol: captured pre-restart boot_id and data checksums, rebooted node1, polled until exec returned, confirmed changed boot_id and fresh uptime, and re-verified /srv/data auto-remounted with content still matching the baseline manifest.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed btrfs-progs and loaded btrfs kernel module on node1\",\"Created 2GiB loopback image, formatted btrfs, created 'data' subvolume, mounted at /srv/data\",\"Persisted mount via /etc/fstab (loop,subvol=data) and added btrfs to /etc/modules so it survives reboot\",\"Populated /srv/data with app/config/app.conf and app/uploads/record1.txt, record2.txt\",\"Took read-only btrfs snapshot of /srv/data as baseline; saved sha256 manifest\",\"Modified /srv/data (edited app.conf, deleted record2.txt, added junk.txt) confirming drift via manifest diff\",\"Restored /srv/data to exact baseline snapshot via subvolume swap (mv corrupted subvol aside, snapshot baseline as new 'data' subvol, remount); verified byte-identical via sha256 diff\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and data health proof\",\"Issued native reboot on node1, polled until exec available again\",\"Confirmed changed boot_id and fresh uptime post-restart\",\"Re-verified /srv/data auto-mounted via fstab post-reboot with content matching baseline manifest exactly\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Filesystem snapshot capability established for /srv/data (btrfs subvolume + loop-mounted fs)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-999489317dfb491a\",\"cmd-d43769d7f2b04f4b\",\"cmd-70ee206a9c7549dd\",\"cmd-f044664548e24fc6\",\"cmd-ab24694ba6b84db1\",\"cmd-3f3bc0d51ae14993\"],\"summary\":\"btrfs-progs installed, btrfs module loaded, loopback device formatted as btrfs with a 'data' subvolume mounted at /srv/data, persisted via /etc/fstab and confirmed via mount -a\"},{\"requirement\":\"Baseline data populated and snapshot captured\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a4990a4c7c8846d3\",\"cmd-699c54143e37459f\",\"cmd-85cb29a3fe8a42d5\"],\"summary\":\"Created app.conf, record1.txt, record2.txt under /srv/data, recorded sha256 checksums, then created a read-only btrfs snapshot and confirmed its content matches the live data manifest\"},{\"requirement\":\"Directory modified after snapshot (edit/delete/add)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-639ab9303d294c29\"],\"summary\":\"app.conf overwritten, record2.txt deleted, junk.txt added; diff against baseline manifest shows the drift\"},{\"requirement\":\"Exact restore of earlier snapshot content\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ce131752e18a469e\",\"cmd-b4c41e49a2f94d72\"],\"summary\":\"Live subvolume swapped for a writable snapshot of the read-only baseline snapshot; post-restore sha256 manifest diff against baseline manifest is empty (byte-identical), junk.txt gone, record2.txt and app.conf restored\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline captured for node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f835231c5eb94191\",\"cmd-059b3bcad1994b1d\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 7d560aac-09ed-4407-810c-51eb86900733, uptime start, fstab entry, live mount, file listing, checksums, and btrfs subvolume list prior to reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity for node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a69c142d5b5644bc\",\"cmd-59c625b93ed1479c\",\"cmd-e5be4513c33646aa\",\"cmd-4250494b522b41c3\",\"cmd-0b6725840c904f0d\",\"cmd-f4ce7a130d5d4011\",\"cmd-41d8a6950d034041\",\"cmd-bdce1f5b6bb24d03\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot command acknowledged and returned before disconnect; subsequent polls show connection reset/timeout during res